NAME
    freeze - pin a memory value across frames

SYNOPSIS
    freeze add <space> <addr> [<value>] [-w 1|2|4] [--le|--be] [--dec|--float] [--json]
    freeze list [--json]
    freeze remove <id> [--json]
    freeze clear [--json]

DESCRIPTION
    Pins hex address <addr> (width 1, 2, or 4 bytes; default 1, or 4 with
    --float) in writable memory space <space> to <value>, or snapshots the
    live value at <addr> when <value> is omitted. Endianness defaults to
    the space's hardware byte order unless overridden with --le or --be.
    Read-only memory spaces are refused.

    Crystal checks active freezes once per frame at frame end and writes
    the pinned bytes back whenever any byte in the span differs from the
    pinned representation. 'freeze list' reports 'blocked' as the count of
    frames whose end found the pinned value modified; for immediate
    execution-time write interception or instruction PC attribution, use
    watch(1) or 'bp write' in bp(1).

OPTIONS
    add <space> <addr> [<value>] [-w 1|2|4] [--le|--be] [--dec|--float] [--json]
        Freeze 1, 2, or 4 bytes at <addr> in <space> to <value> (or
        snapshot the current value when <value> is omitted).

    list [--json]
        List active freezes with their IDs, targets, values, widths,
        byte orders, and blocked counts.

    remove <id> [--json]
        Remove freeze #<id>.

    clear [--json]
        Remove all active freezes.

EXAMPLES
    freeze add WRAM 13c6
    freeze add WRAM 0dbf 63
    freeze add RDRAM 100 999 -w 2 --be --dec --json
    freeze list --json
    freeze remove 1
    freeze clear

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage/refusal message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid argument, or session
        service fault.

SEE ALSO
    cheat(1), watch(1), search(1), counters(1), spaces(1)
